 return [h('6. Supporting document' if section else 'Technical report'),p('Resume Studio: AI-Powered Resume Feedback & Gap Analysis','h1'),p('Promptlytics | PE-B49-20 | Batch 56\nFaculty: Ankit Vijay Bansal | Leader: Akshat Garag','small'),p('Architecture and scope','h3'),p('A static GitHub Pages application provides a resume workspace, prompt lab, evidence dashboard and team view. Browser JavaScript performs local skill coverage and evidence validation. A lazy-loaded WebLLM bundle can run SmolLM2 on a compatible WebGPU device. Optional Gemini calls use a user key held in tab memory, or a loopback-only Node server with an environment key. There is no database, agent loop or retrieval pipeline.'),p('Prompt design and actual experiment','h3'),p('One final prompt P1 v3 compares the same source pair, requests exact evidence quotes, rewrites only factual bullets and returns five JSON fields. The full prompt includes one fictional example. Three independent Codex research-agent sessions ran T01 on 24 November 2026. v1 returned free text, v2 returned JSON with differing field shapes, and v3 met the final contract. The runtime described a GPT-6 family assistant; exact backend identifier and temperature were not exposed. One sample per version cannot establish general performance gains.'),p('Data handling','h3'),p('Local analysis and manual validation keep source text in the current tab. On-device inference downloads model files, which may be cached, while resume text stays local. Gemini is an explicit opt-in and sends text and a user key to Google. No key is included in public source or application storage. Reports and prompt downloads can contain supplied text. Remove private details before sharing them.'),PageBreak(),h('Technical report - results and limitations'),table(['Evidence','Observed result'],[['Local capability evaluation','12 inputs: 11 pass, 1 experience-depth limitation'],['Input categories','4 Normal; 5 Edge; 3 Invalid'],['Regression tests','17 pass, including mocked provider transport'],['Prompt experiments','3 actual independent assistant-session responses; final contract results: fail / fail / pass'],['On-device generation','SmolLM2-360M first omitted matched_skills; structured decoding then passed the contract. A weak JavaScript quote still required human review.'],['Video demonstration',str(round(reel['duration_seconds'],2))+' seconds, captioned real browser capture']],[155,335]),Spacer(1,15),p('Limitations and next actions','h3'),p('1. Keyword presence cannot establish years or depth of experience (T08). Add labeled semantic evaluation.\n2. Common explicit negation is handled; complex negation and mixed statements can still fail. Expand adversarial inputs.\n3. Exact quotes and numeric checks do not prove entailment or catch every invented nonnumeric claim. Keep human review.\n4. Small on-device models can produce poor or incomplete structures, and WebGPU support varies. Treat output as a draft and retain manual or own-key alternatives.'),p('Reproducibility','h3'),p('Run npm test and npm run evaluate. Saved inputs, full outputs and failures are in test-data/. Prompt experiment JSON records include the rendered prompt, actual response, tool, settings and validation result. Tests use fictional data. Contributions are assigned ownership of an AI-assisted build; all-member agreement is not claimed.'),p('Source and access','h3'),p(repo+'\n'+site,'small'),p('Runtime references: https://webllm.mlc.ai/docs/ and https://aistudio.google.com/api-reference/generate-content','small')]

